# What the image builds do NOT need.
#
# Every service except the frontend builds from the repo root, so without
# this file `docker compose build` ships the entire working tree as build
# context. That was 53GB here (dev/uxtest-data alone is 42GB), which does
# not fail loudly: BuildKit stalls, the classic builder streams gigabytes
# for many minutes, and the stale image stays in place while the build
# reports success.
#
# Keep in mind when editing: the five root-context Dockerfiles copy
# VERSION, alembic.ini, alembic/, integrations/, pyproject.toml,
# services/ and shared/. In particular services/perception/models/ holds
# the YOLO, easyocr and insightface weights and must stay in the context.

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode

# Python local environments and caches
.venv
.venv-*
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Other apps that build from their own context, or not at all
frontend
mobile

# Test and development fixtures. dev/uxtest-data is written by the
# ux-army scheduled runs and grows without bound.
tests
dev
docs

# Runtime data written by a running stack, never an input to a build
recordings
thumbnails
logs
data
*.log

# Local config and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
